  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "lqF59jZNoSfzfOnKmQCBH0Wv1ps=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:50.462Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Flowable AG is headquartered in Zurich with an office in Berlin, offers first-party *\"Cloud-based\"*, *\"On-premise\"* and *\"Hybrid\"* deployment, holds SOC 2, ISO 27001 and GDPR compliance, and names government among its verticals.\n\nThe screening rule this corpus uses is that where a vendor has filled the gap, the only remaining opening is that the occupying solution cannot be procured under EU or German public-sector rules. A Swiss vendor with a German office selling an on-premise deployment under ISO 27001 does not create that opening.\n\nWhat remains is a commercial objection \u2014 Enterprise costs money \u2014 which means competing on price and features against an incumbent with 600-plus enterprise customers in its own category. That is a different and much harder proposition than filling an empty slot, and it is the basis for the DEAD END verdict.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:50.462728Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:50.462732Z"
    }
  },
